### The Anomaly
While parsing open data extracts for the City Budget Explorer, our automated checksum pipeline threw continuous balance validation errors. The declared municipal total was $58.4M, but summing the departmental sub-tables produced only $56.1M.

### The Investigation
After auditing each capital allocation line item, we discovered that off-balance contingency fund expenditures were included in the summary headline figure but excluded from the department-level breakdown CSV.

```javascript
// Automated reconciliation validator
const subtotal = rows.reduce((acc, r) => acc + Number(r.amount), 0);
const discrepancy = Math.abs(subtotal - summaryTotal);
if (discrepancy > 1000) {
  reportDiscrepancy({ expected: summaryTotal, actual: subtotal, delta: discrepancy });
}
```

### Public Impact
We published our automated reconciliation audit to the city comptroller's public comments desk. Two weeks later, the data portal released an amended export format documenting the capital reserve lines.

